And what was it that Fr. Cicero told you?

2237
01:58:12,598 --> 01:58:13,598
He Said like this...

2238
01:58:13,708 --> 01:58:17,215
"That little harmonica I
blessed before I died"

2239
01:58:17,556 --> 01:58:21,539
"deliver it to Severino, who
needs it much more than you do."

2240
01:58:21,564 --> 01:58:22,788
My God!

2241
01:58:23,444 --> 01:58:25,515
It just might have been
my godfather Fr. Cicero.

2242
01:58:25,748 --> 01:58:28,333
With a harmonica of deforestation, even
I will like to kill these people!

2243
01:58:28,648 --> 01:58:30,836
João, give me that harmonica.

2244
01:58:30,861 --> 01:58:32,173
So let me go and let Chicó go.

2245
01:58:32,198 --> 01:58:33,370
It can not be, João.

2246
01:58:33,682 --> 01:58:36,236
I killed the baker, the woman,
the bishop and the priest...

2247
01:58:36,261 --> 01:58:38,102
and they died waiting for you.

2248
01:58:38,480 --> 01:58:39,525
If I don't kill you,

2249
01:58:39,550 --> 01:58:42,599
they come at night to chase me,
because it will be an injustice to them.

2250
01:58:42,605 --> 01:58:45,728
I give you an opportunity to
meet my godfather Padim Ciço,

2251
01:58:46,067 --> 01:58:47,885
and you pay me this way?

2252
01:58:48,129 --> 01:58:51,405
To meet my padinho?
I was never that lucky.

2253
01:58:51,752 --> 01:58:53,012
But you can meet him now.

2254
01:58:53,108 --> 01:58:55,707
- How?
- A man shoots you with a rifle...

2255
01:58:55,805 --> 01:58:58,641
you will visit him. I play
on the harmonica and you come back.

2256
01:58:58,650 --> 01:59:02,216
- And if you don't play?
- Can't you see that I don't make such a misery?

2257
01:59:02,279 --> 01:59:05,054
- I guarantee I do.
- Your idea is good, but just to be safe...

2258
01:59:05,055 --> 01:59:06,403
give the harmonica to my man soon.

2259
01:59:07,715 --> 01:59:10,371
- Now I get shot and see my padinho?
- See.

2260
01:59:10,712 --> 01:59:12,958
- Could't you see, Chico?
- I saw a lot.

2261
01:59:13,195 --> 01:59:16,391
He is there, dressed in blue, with
a lot of little angels around.

2262
01:59:16,416 --> 01:59:19,198
He said like this: "Tell
Severino that I want to see him".

2263
01:59:19,223 --> 01:59:20,100
Oh, I will!

2264
01:59:20,653 --> 01:59:22,662
- Shoot!
- Captain...

2265
01:59:22,687 --> 01:59:24,259
Shoot, loose man,
Am I not ordering it?

2266
01:59:24,259 --> 01:59:27,025
Captain, let's go that the steering wheel
must have already been warned.

2267
01:59:27,025 --> 01:59:27,796
- Shoot!

2268
01:59:27,821 --> 01:59:29,806
Man, shoot at once,
for God's sake!

2269
01:59:30,174 --> 01:59:32,776
I don't like it, but if I must...

2270
01:59:32,801 --> 01:59:33,516
Wait!

2271
01:59:34,935 --> 01:59:38,303
- Don't forget the harmonica.
- Don't worry, captain!

2272
01:59:40,550 --> 01:59:41,582
So shoot!

2273
01:59:45,148 --> 01:59:47,047
The police are coming!

2274
01:59:53,017 --> 01:59:53,647
- Captain?

2275
01:59:53,647 --> 01:59:56,081
- Leave him a little longer!

2276
01:59:56,829 --> 01:59:58,328
Come on, captain!

2277
01:59:59,551 --> 02:00:00,961
Captain!

2278
02:00:01,876 --> 02:00:05,154
Damn you! You killed the captain,
didn't you?

2279
02:00:06,185 --> 02:00:07,398
Do you want some killing?

2280
02:00:08,347 --> 02:00:10,085
Take this, bunch of monkeys!

2281
02:00:12,743 --> 02:00:15,224
- Come on, João!
- I'm taking the money with me!

2282
02:00:15,249 --> 02:00:16,465
Run!

2283
02:00:17,584 --> 02:00:21,129
Bastard! For once in my life,
I'll enjoy killing someone!

2284
02:00:37,137 --> 02:00:38,137
João!

2285
02:00:40,278 --> 02:00:43,308
João! João! Are you dieing?

2286
02:00:43,983 --> 02:00:45,196
I think I am, Chicó.

2287
02:00:47,720 --> 02:00:49,050
Things are blurry.

2288
02:00:49,075 --> 02:00:52,649
Poor João's going to die.

2289
02:00:52,674 --> 02:00:54,515
Quit the whining, Chicó.

2290
02:00:55,174 --> 02:00:56,943
You've seen a man die before.

2291
02:00:57,959 --> 02:01:00,388
The only thing I regret
is not getting the money...

2292
02:01:00,413 --> 02:01:03,602
I'd get when
you marry Rosinha.

2293
02:01:12,608 --> 02:01:13,440
João...

2294
02:01:14,611 --> 02:01:15,611
João!

2295
02:01:15,636 --> 02:01:16,636
João!

2296
02:01:16,886 --> 02:01:17,886
João!

2297
02:01:18,432 --> 02:01:19,529
João!

2298
02:01:23,614 --> 02:01:24,760
Oh, God!

2299
02:01:26,480 --> 02:01:28,504
Poor João Grilo is dead!

2300
02:01:30,868 --> 02:01:34,617
What a bastard,
to die like this!

2301
02:01:37,101 --> 02:01:39,401
What am I going to
do without João?

2302
02:01:39,452 --> 02:01:41,492
What am I going to
do without João?

2303
02:01:43,521 --> 02:01:45,311
João! João!

2304
02:01:48,515 --> 02:01:50,014
There's no undoing this.

2305
02:01:52,503 --> 02:01:54,089
João Grilo is dead.

2306
02:02:08,472 --> 02:02:11,522
The world's smartest
Grilo is gone.

2307
02:02:15,216 --> 02:02:17,197
He fulfilled his fate...

2308
02:02:18,164 --> 02:02:20,951
met the irreparable doom...

2309
02:02:21,562 --> 02:02:24,723
which marks our strange
destiny on this Earth...

2310
02:02:25,801 --> 02:02:27,682
the unexplainable fact...

2311
02:02:28,785 --> 02:02:32,390
which puts all living things in one
flock of condemned creatures...

2312
02:02:34,115 --> 02:02:35,647
because all that lives...

2313
02:02:37,893 --> 02:02:38,706
shall die.

2314
02:02:53,730 --> 02:02:59,781
<i>Hail, Mary</i>

2315
02:02:59,887 --> 02:03:05,192
<i>Hail, hail</i>

2316
02:03:05,217 --> 02:03:10,733
<i>Hail, Mary</i>

2317
02:03:10,758 --> 02:03:15,793
<i>Make your penitence</i>

2318
02:03:15,818 --> 02:03:20,708
<i>For all your sins</i>

2319
02:03:20,733 --> 02:03:25,787
<i>And tell Holy Mary</i>

2320
02:03:25,812 --> 02:03:31,004
<i>To came and embrace you</i>

2321
02:03:34,720 --> 02:03:36,983
João! You rotten bastard!

2322
02:03:37,008 --> 02:03:38,662
I don't believe it!

2323
02:03:39,511 --> 02:03:42,096
Not even here
you get off my back?

2324
02:03:42,121 --> 02:03:44,994
I've looked around,
but I haven't seen Father Cicero.

2325
02:03:45,019 --> 02:03:47,175
- He's got many people to see!
- You're right.

2326
02:03:47,200 --> 02:03:50,076
- It's crowded in here!

2327
02:03:50,101 --> 02:03:51,101
- And there are more coming.

2328
02:03:51,200 --> 02:03:53,227
Look at the four you dispatched.

2329
02:03:56,663 --> 02:03:59,766
There must be a special
place for the clergy.

2330
02:04:00,106 --> 02:04:02,972
By the way,
why aren't you down there?

2331
02:04:02,997 --> 02:04:06,945
- I'm dead, like you.
- I'm no man to die!

2332
02:04:06,970 --> 02:04:08,811
- Remember the harmonica?

2333
02:04:09,400 --> 02:04:10,510
- I do...

2334
02:04:10,601 --> 02:04:12,946
What are my man doing...

2335
02:04:12,970 --> 02:04:15,315
Why doesn't my man play it,
so I can go back?

2336
02:04:15,340 --> 02:04:17,103
Old fool!

2337
02:04:17,216 --> 02:04:19,524
Do you think a harmonica
can make you live?

2338
02:04:19,549 --> 02:04:21,766
Watch your mouth or I kill you!

2339
02:04:21,794 --> 02:04:23,699
How?
I'm already dead!

2340
02:04:27,162 --> 02:04:31,181
He's not the only one!
I'll kill anyone who laughs!

2341
02:04:31,206 --> 02:04:33,412
- We meant no offense.

2342
02:04:33,437 --> 02:04:35,684
- But you didn't die alone.

2343
02:04:35,709 --> 02:04:38,490
- We've all died.
- As Chicó used to say...

2344
02:04:38,515 --> 02:04:42,910
"We fulfilled our fates and
met the irreparable doom."

2345
02:04:43,041 --> 02:04:45,507
- Where's Chicó?
- He escaped.

2346
02:04:45,532 --> 02:04:48,378
He's alive, that rascal!
Hell of a guy!

2347
02:04:48,403 --> 02:04:51,332
- He was the only one!
- As he used to say...

2348
02:04:51,357 --> 02:04:55,102
It's the first time I hear
the dead quote the living!

2349
02:04:55,185 --> 02:04:57,646
You'll pay me for this
harmonica trick, you bastard!

2350
02:04:57,671 --> 02:04:59,611
Bastard my butt!

2351
02:04:59,636 --> 02:05:02,542
I'm already dead!
I won't listen to this!

2352
02:05:02,567 --> 02:05:04,747
There's no rich or poor,
brave or coward.

2353
02:05:04,772 --> 02:05:06,989
We're all equals before God...

2354
02:05:07,349 --> 02:05:08,349
Or the devil!

2355
02:05:12,888 --> 02:05:15,784
Why are you all so surprised?

2356
02:05:18,618 --> 02:05:19,618
The door!

2357
02:05:21,875 --> 02:05:24,778
Am I a monster,
by any chance?

2358
02:05:25,299 --> 02:05:26,905
Not at all!

2359
02:05:26,930 --> 02:05:30,813
Your elegance impresses us!

2360
02:05:31,093 --> 02:05:34,871
- You look like a movie star.
- Do you think so?

2361
02:05:34,896 --> 02:05:36,931
- I do.
- Then I do too.

2362
02:05:36,956 --> 02:05:40,594
Has anyone ever told you
you're much nicer in person?

2363
02:05:40,846 --> 02:05:44,994
And I don't usually like
people at first.

2364
02:05:45,100 --> 02:05:49,582
See? The devil isn't
as ugly as they say.

2365
02:05:51,828 --> 02:05:54,416
Okay, but this smell of sulfur...

2366
02:05:56,838 --> 02:05:59,912
Is my smell bothering you?

2367
02:06:00,114 --> 02:06:01,236
Oh, no, no.

2368
02:06:01,261 --> 02:06:03,743
It's quite nice!

2369
02:06:04,212 --> 02:06:07,013
I'm about to faint
because of the smell!

2370
02:06:07,294 --> 02:06:11,100
Watch it!
Be respectful.

2371
02:06:11,125 --> 02:06:12,702
But what is this, creature?

2372
02:06:12,727 --> 02:06:15,639
- We mean no disrespect!
- I'll let it pass for this time.

2373
02:06:15,664 --> 02:06:18,101
You should thank God
the devil's a nice guy.

2374
02:06:18,393 --> 02:06:19,922
- If I were him...
- lf I were him...

2375
02:06:19,947 --> 02:06:23,709
I'd wash real hard
to get rid of this stench!

2376
02:06:26,810 --> 02:06:29,510
You're going to pay
for everything you did!

2377
02:06:29,535 --> 02:06:31,783
I love a tough man!

2378
02:06:31,808 --> 02:06:35,197
I'm going to send you all to hell!

2379
02:06:37,456 --> 02:06:38,720
We're screwed!

2380
02:06:40,875 --> 02:06:42,701
See what you've done?

2381
02:06:42,726 --> 02:06:45,573
I wanted him to show us
his true face!

2382
02:06:49,108 --> 02:06:51,781
Now, we know who
we're talking to!

2383
02:06:51,806 --> 02:06:56,826
We're all going
to the eternal fire...

2384
02:06:56,851 --> 02:06:59,292
to suffer with me!

2385
02:06:59,709 --> 02:07:02,944
You think we'll go,
just because you said so?

2386
02:07:03,102 --> 02:07:07,337
That's right,
and there's no way out!

2387
02:07:16,566 --> 02:07:19,340
What a hell of court is this,
with no right to an appeal?

2388
02:07:19,576 --> 02:07:22,205
A person has to be heard...

2389
02:07:22,311 --> 02:07:23,991
before he's convicted!

2390
02:07:24,186 --> 02:07:27,030
- Nonsense, foolishness!

2391
02:07:27,055 --> 02:07:28,511
It may be so...

2392
02:07:28,795 --> 02:07:30,791
but I appeal
to the Mighty One!

2393
02:07:30,923 --> 02:07:34,309
Help me, My Lord
Jesus Christ!

2394
02:07:52,201 --> 02:07:54,876
Who is it?
Emmanuel?

2395
02:07:55,251 --> 02:07:58,975
Yes, it's Emmanuel, the Lion
of Judah, the son of David.

2396
02:07:59,194 --> 02:08:02,297
Come all, for you shall be judged.

2397
02:08:07,877 --> 02:08:10,716
I mean no disrespect
to such an important person...

2398
02:08:10,780 --> 02:08:14,028
but that guy just
called you Emmanuel.

2399
02:08:14,053 --> 02:08:16,415
That's right, João.
That's one of my names.

2400
02:08:16,579 --> 02:08:19,750
But you can also call me
Jesus, Lord, God.

2401
02:08:19,775 --> 02:08:22,664
Hold on a minute!
Are you Jesus?

2402
02:08:22,689 --> 02:08:23,983
Yes, why?

2403
02:08:24,112 --> 02:08:27,185
Because... No disrespect...

2404
02:08:27,420 --> 02:08:30,184
but I didn't think you'd be
so brown!

2405
02:08:30,386 --> 02:08:32,371
- Hush!
- You hush.

2406
02:08:32,671 --> 02:08:36,198
You were more astounded
than him, but didn't show it...

2407
02:08:36,265 --> 02:08:37,804
out of worldly arrogance.

2408
02:08:37,829 --> 02:08:41,210
- The time of falsehood is over.
- Well said!

2409
02:08:41,250 --> 02:08:44,361
The color may not be the best,
but you're very good with words!

2410
02:08:44,386 --> 02:08:46,684
Thank you, João.

2411
02:08:46,885 --> 02:08:50,454
But you yourself are
prejudiced towards race.

2412
02:08:50,691 --> 02:08:54,695
I came like this on purpose.
I knew I'd get a reaction.

2413
02:08:55,713 --> 02:08:59,452
And you, quit imitating my looks!

2414
02:08:59,477 --> 02:09:03,104
You know you're not equal to God.

2415
02:09:03,347 --> 02:09:04,886
Big Deal!

2416
02:09:06,656 --> 02:09:09,501
- Now stop the story and turn around.
- I'm fine like this.

2417
02:09:09,730 --> 02:09:12,521
As you wish.
Make your report...

2418
02:09:13,014 --> 02:09:14,014
starting with the bishop.

2419
02:09:16,014 --> 02:09:21,509
Simony. Negotiated with the Corporal, approving
the burial of a dog in Latin,

2420
02:09:21,534 --> 02:09:23,964
because the owner gave him six contos.

2421
02:09:24,092 --> 02:09:27,375
- And is it forbidden?
- Man! Whether it's forbidden I don't know.

2422
02:09:27,496 --> 02:09:30,405
What I do know is that how thought you were,

2423
02:09:30,430 --> 02:09:33,708
and then suddenly
started to think it wasn't.

2424
02:09:33,991 --> 02:09:34,991
And more!

2425
02:09:36,386 --> 02:09:40,081
Rascality.
Arrogance with the little ones.

2426
02:09:40,209 --> 02:09:42,559
Subservience with the greats.

2427
02:09:42,665 --> 02:09:46,687
And whatever is said of the bishop,
can apply to the priest.

2428
02:09:46,770 --> 02:09:50,461
But I didn't quote the
false canonical  code like him.

2429
02:09:50,535 --> 02:09:55,039
On the other hand, it has just incurred
lacking in collegiality with the bishop.

2430
02:09:55,175 --> 02:09:58,264
Boy!
What I do here is still vogue?

2431
02:09:58,297 --> 02:10:01,685
No. This is the Devil's confusion.

2432
02:10:01,946 --> 02:10:03,979
- And the baker?
- He and his wife...

2433
02:10:04,004 --> 02:10:06,546
were the worst bosses
that Taperoá has ever seen.

2434
02:10:06,571 --> 02:10:09,351
- It's a lie!
- Not. It is true!

2435
02:10:09,682 --> 02:10:10,628
Three days I spent...

2436
02:10:10,628 --> 02:10:13,978
"On top of a bed with a fever and not a
little cup of water they sent him."

2437
02:10:13,978 --> 02:10:14,978
I already know, João.

2438
02:10:15,701 --> 02:10:19,652
Everyone knows this story
from hearing you telling so much.

2439
02:10:19,795 --> 02:10:22,187
But can I?
Tell me even if can I?

2440
02:10:22,212 --> 02:10:25,209
Steak in butter for the dog
and hunger for João Grilo?

2441
02:10:25,387 --> 02:10:27,890
- It's too much!
- Husband's greed.

2442
02:10:28,020 --> 02:10:35,213
The wife, an adulteress. If you place it on a scale,
they were both terrible.

2443
02:10:35,326 --> 02:10:37,816
- Accuse Severino.
- Do I have to?

2444
02:10:39,306 --> 02:10:41,781
He killed more than 30 people!

2445
02:10:41,806 --> 02:10:44,552
This devil is everything
I've always hated...

2446
02:10:44,640 --> 02:10:47,505
a DA, a sacristan,
a dog, and a policeman.

2447
02:10:47,660 --> 02:10:49,596
You're being funny, now...

2448
02:10:49,778 --> 02:10:54,364
but Emmanuel is fair. Things
look good for me, not for you.

2449
02:10:54,498 --> 02:10:59,007
That's true. Things look bad.
The charges are serious.

2450
02:11:00,538 --> 02:11:02,784
What amuses me the most...

2451
02:11:02,998 --> 02:11:06,720
is seeing this coward
shaking with fear.

2452
02:11:08,623 --> 02:11:12,099
I can't help it! If I could
stop shaking, I'd defend myself!

2453
02:11:12,263 --> 02:11:13,263
Stop!

2454
02:11:14,349 --> 02:11:16,874
What a relief!
I was getting tired.

2455
02:11:17,398 --> 02:11:19,761
- What was that?
- One of the devil's tricks.

2456
02:11:19,901 --> 02:11:23,597
He likes playing games.

2457
02:11:23,785 --> 02:11:26,773
It could only have been
that mischief-maker!

2458
02:11:26,798 --> 02:11:28,918
What do you say
in your defense?

2459
02:11:29,117 --> 02:11:33,504
I know you're clever, but
you know you've been accused.

2460
02:11:33,529 --> 02:11:36,504
Actually, I haven't
been accused of anything!

2461
02:11:36,529 --> 02:11:38,495
- No?
- No, he hasn't!

2462
02:11:38,520 --> 02:11:41,685
He made such a fuss that
I forgot to accuse him.

2463
02:11:41,772 --> 02:11:44,998
But I'll get you now,
you rascal.

2464
02:11:45,236 --> 02:11:49,193
He plotted the
bitch's funeral...

2465
02:11:49,551 --> 02:11:52,604
inciting simony.

2466
02:11:53,058 --> 02:11:57,702
Sold a cat to the baker's wife
saying that he put money,

2467
02:11:58,099 --> 02:12:01,304
embezzlement.

2468
02:12:02,114 --> 02:12:07,370
He encouraged Chicó
to be with a married woman...

2469
02:12:07,926 --> 02:12:12,120
inciting concupiscence.

2470
02:12:12,721 --> 02:12:16,111
He devised Severino's death...

2471
02:12:17,778 --> 02:12:21,170
premeditated murder!

2472
02:12:23,414 --> 02:12:27,852
João it seems
you overdid it.

2473
02:12:27,877 --> 02:12:30,624
His case is hopeless...

2474
02:12:32,157 --> 02:12:34,157
so I'll take him first.

2475
02:12:34,738 --> 02:12:36,664
I haven't given up!

2476
02:12:36,744 --> 02:12:38,589
I may go, but not that easily!

2477
02:12:38,897 --> 02:12:41,584
- I will appeal!
- To whom, João?

2478
02:12:41,815 --> 02:12:45,414
Even the Lord said
the charges are serious.

2479
02:12:45,910 --> 02:12:46,910
Wait.

2480
02:12:48,680 --> 02:12:49,767
- To whom will you appeal?

2481
02:12:49,767 --> 02:12:51,870
- To someone closer to us.

2482
02:12:51,941 --> 02:12:53,434
- Someone who watches us.

2483
02:12:53,507 --> 02:12:54,507
- A saint?

2484
02:12:54,612 --> 02:12:56,898
I may look stupid, but I'm not.

2485
02:12:56,923 --> 02:12:58,788
I have a higher card.

2486
02:12:59,022 --> 02:12:59,864
Who's that?

2487
02:13:00,307 --> 02:13:02,603
"Hail Mary, save us all
Hear us when we call

2488
02:13:02,628 --> 02:13:04,968
Milk from the gentle cow
From the stubborn, not now

2489
02:13:04,993 --> 02:13:07,446
The gentle one has calmed down
The stubborn one put her foot down

2490
02:13:07,471 --> 02:13:09,730
I was once a brand new boat
The finest ship afloat

2491
02:13:09,755 --> 02:13:12,213
I've been a boy and man
I haven't been a woman yet

2492
02:13:12,238 --> 02:13:15,578
Aid me Blessed Virgin
Mother of God of Nazareth!"

2493
02:13:29,650 --> 02:13:31,612
Here comes the Compassionate.

2494
02:13:31,884 --> 02:13:33,733
Women meddle in everything!

2495
02:13:36,350 --> 02:13:40,671
How did you look beautiful
with that color, My Son.

2496
02:13:41,900 --> 02:13:43,172
But a little thin.

2497
02:13:44,532 --> 02:13:47,496
You did call me,
didn't you, João?

2498
02:13:47,831 --> 02:13:50,111
- Did my verse anger you?

2499
02:13:50,136 --> 02:13:53,192
- No, João. Why would I be?

2500
02:13:54,092 --> 02:13:56,007
They were funny,
and that is good.

2501
02:13:57,812 --> 02:13:59,707
It's the devil
who likes gloom.

2502
02:14:00,446 --> 02:14:02,348
- I object!
- I know you do, but I'm sorry.

2503
02:14:02,348 --> 02:14:05,310
I can't go against My Mother.

2504
02:14:05,904 --> 02:14:09,290
Big deal her habit
of saving everyone!

2505
02:14:09,432 --> 02:14:11,382
It demoralizes everything.

2506
02:14:11,407 --> 02:14:14,294
- That's because you had no mother!
- That's right!

2507
02:14:14,319 --> 02:14:17,320
Such a mean fellow must've
come from an incubator!

2508
02:14:18,001 --> 02:14:19,776
Why did you call me?

2509
02:14:19,863 --> 02:14:22,576
This son of an incubator
wants to take us to hell.

2510
02:14:22,625 --> 02:14:24,782
I had to appeal to you.

2511
02:14:25,424 --> 02:14:26,971
I'll see what I can do.

2512
02:14:28,992 --> 02:14:31,340
I plea for these poor souls...

2513
02:14:32,281 --> 02:14:33,653
for they have no one.

2514
02:14:35,599 --> 02:14:36,799
Don't condemn them.

2515
02:14:37,017 --> 02:14:39,970
- I appeal to justice!
- And I, to mercy.

2516
02:14:39,995 --> 02:14:44,201
We must consider the poor
and sad condition of man.

2517
02:14:44,727 --> 02:14:47,319
It all starts with fear.

2518
02:14:47,642 --> 02:14:50,797
Because of it, men commit
evil deeds, almost unwittingly.

2519
02:14:52,508 --> 02:14:55,263
- It's fear.
- What do they fear?

2520
02:14:56,732 --> 02:14:58,308
They fear many things...

2521
02:14:59,885 --> 02:15:00,885
suffering...

2522
02:15:02,656 --> 02:15:03,656
loneliness...

2523
02:15:05,210 --> 02:15:08,704
and, above all,
they fear death.

2524
02:15:09,699 --> 02:15:12,298
And you tell me that?

2525
02:15:13,356 --> 02:15:15,071
Me, who died alone, abandoned...

2526
02:15:18,704 --> 02:15:20,391
even by My Father.

2527
02:15:21,648 --> 02:15:24,223
Don't forget the night
you spent in the garden...

2528
02:15:25,508 --> 02:15:27,817
the fear you underwent.

2529
02:15:28,743 --> 02:15:29,743
Poor man!

2530
02:15:31,049 --> 02:15:33,592
Made of flesh and blood,
like any other man.

2531
02:15:34,948 --> 02:15:40,383
Like all men, you were left
alone to die and to suffer.

2532
02:15:40,613 --> 02:15:45,603
Everybody fears death, but that
doesn't make them righteous.

2533
02:15:46,107 --> 02:15:48,687
How did this fear make the baker
and his wife...

2534
02:15:48,712 --> 02:15:50,879
better people?

2535
02:15:51,615 --> 02:15:55,896
Fear of death alone
does not redeem sins.

2536
02:15:56,205 --> 02:15:58,327
But it may,
at the time of death.

2537
02:16:00,120 --> 02:16:05,266
In the Hail Mary, I am asked to
pray for men when they die.

2538
02:16:07,288 --> 02:16:11,700
I do.

2539
02:16:13,011 --> 02:16:16,078
And I look unto them at this hour.

2540
02:16:16,376 --> 02:16:19,629
Often, it is when they die that they finally find what they'd
been looking for all their lives.

2541
02:16:21,625 --> 02:16:23,409
That's what happened
to Eurico and Dora...

2542
02:16:24,001 --> 02:16:26,672
when they were about to be shot.

2543
02:16:32,427 --> 02:16:35,918
Stand here.
I'll shoot from the church.

2544
02:16:36,207 --> 02:16:37,562
You'll have time
for a Hail Mary.

2545
02:16:37,617 --> 02:16:39,086
I'll pray too,

2546
02:16:39,111 --> 02:16:41,063
and she'll hear us.

2547
02:16:43,434 --> 02:16:46,602
We always think we can
live a little longer.

2548
02:16:49,701 --> 02:16:51,605
I like living...

2549
02:16:53,220 --> 02:16:57,274
but I've always asked myself if
I wanted to live longer than you.

2550
02:16:59,335 --> 02:17:00,636
Now, I know.

2551
02:17:01,774 --> 02:17:03,629
I couldn't stand to see you die.

2552
02:17:07,937 --> 02:17:10,783
- I want to die first, Eurico!
- Oh, Dora!

2553
02:17:13,202 --> 02:17:15,089
Why did you cheat on me
all this time?

2554
02:17:18,886 --> 02:17:20,695
That was the reason...

2555
02:17:21,719 --> 02:17:25,192
It was like killing you
in my heart little by little.

2556
02:17:25,614 --> 02:17:27,544
I was so afraid of losing you,

2557
02:17:27,603 --> 02:17:29,614
I wanted it to happen slowly!

2558
02:17:30,439 --> 02:17:34,558
Don't worry.
Now, we'll be together forever.

2559
02:17:36,813 --> 02:17:40,294
Hey, mister,
we have one last wish.

2560
02:17:44,101 --> 02:17:47,173
- We want to die together.
- Good, it'll save me a bullet...

2561
02:17:47,198 --> 02:17:49,126
it's one less for my record.

2562
02:17:58,102 --> 02:17:59,980
I claim, in their favor...

2563
02:18:00,902 --> 02:18:03,727
the husband's forgiveness
at the time of their death...

2564
02:18:04,578 --> 02:18:07,066
when he put his arms around her,
so they could die together.

2565
02:18:10,642 --> 02:18:14,179
He was the greatest
victim of her actions...

2566
02:18:15,327 --> 02:18:18,100
and, yet, he prayed for her.

2567
02:18:18,550 --> 02:18:22,299
I note your plea. What about
the Bishop and the priest?

2568
02:18:23,012 --> 02:18:26,100
They also had their revelation
at the time of death.

2569
02:18:30,856 --> 02:18:33,086
It's bad luck to kill a priest.

2570
02:18:33,395 --> 02:18:36,450
- Especially for the priest!
- Before I shoot...

2571
02:18:36,475 --> 02:18:38,785
I want your absolution.

2572
02:18:39,241 --> 02:18:43,679
To be forgiven,
you must repent first...

2573
02:18:43,738 --> 02:18:45,380
and you can't kill us.

2574
02:18:45,427 --> 02:18:49,273
- I'll repent later!
- Then go repent in hell!

2575
02:18:49,653 --> 02:18:50,877
So there's no way.

2576
02:18:50,902 --> 02:18:54,069
Even if I go to hell,
I have to obey the captain.

2577
02:18:54,094 --> 02:18:56,717
We can't deny absolution.

2578
02:18:57,075 --> 02:18:59,995
We can't bless a killer...

2579
02:19:00,052 --> 02:19:01,569
especially ours!

2580
02:19:02,414 --> 02:19:04,667
We're priests, Your Grace.

2581
02:19:05,167 --> 02:19:09,578
Our mission is to save souls,
even if we can't save our own.

2582
02:19:12,200 --> 02:19:16,102
Remember Jesus' plea
for His executioners!

2583
02:19:17,240 --> 02:19:20,769
Forgive them, Father!

2584
02:19:21,595 --> 02:19:24,247
They don't know
what they're doing!

2585
02:19:44,923 --> 02:19:46,262
My God...

2586
02:19:47,087 --> 02:19:49,499
why have you abandoned us?

2587
02:19:53,240 --> 02:19:55,908
They followed your example...

2588
02:19:56,166 --> 02:19:59,123
...and forgave their killers.
- It's always like that!

2589
02:19:59,177 --> 02:20:01,861
Everyone's good
after they're dead!

2590
02:20:03,498 --> 02:20:06,422
- As for Severino...
- Leave him to me.

2591
02:20:06,447 --> 02:20:09,311
He was redeemed
by his parents' death.

2592
02:20:09,891 --> 02:20:14,106
When he was 8, he faced the beast
that lives in every man.

2593
02:20:26,680 --> 02:20:28,786
I wasn't killed by chance...

2594
02:20:29,053 --> 02:20:31,096
and spent my life
challenging death.

2595
02:20:31,264 --> 02:20:34,549
He went crazy when the
police killed his family.

2596
02:20:34,574 --> 02:20:37,711
He was not responsible
for his actions.

2597
02:20:38,271 --> 02:20:42,392
- He's saved.
- This is an outrage, and I...

2598
02:20:42,417 --> 02:20:44,744
You object, I know.

2599
02:20:44,769 --> 02:20:46,197
But your objection is overruled.

2600
02:20:46,222 --> 02:20:49,210
You don't understand a thing about God's ways.

2601
02:20:51,324 --> 02:20:52,920
Severino is saved.

2602
02:20:52,998 --> 02:20:56,520
He was a mere instrument
of God's wrath.

2603
02:20:56,838 --> 02:21:00,061
Severino, my son,
you can go that way.

2604
02:21:08,537 --> 02:21:09,537
What about us?

2605
02:21:11,603 --> 02:21:16,603
Make up your mind!
This anxiety is worse than anything!

2606
02:21:16,628 --> 02:21:19,742
Don't say that. You don't know
what it's like down there.

2607
02:21:19,767 --> 02:21:23,002
Any anxiety is better than that.

2608
02:21:23,027 --> 02:21:27,995
But I can't wait here forever!

2609
02:21:29,951 --> 02:21:32,785
After all,
what will the sentence be?

2610
02:21:36,478 --> 02:21:39,798
Excuse me, Lord. May I say something?

2611
02:21:39,987 --> 02:21:41,546
- What do you think, mother?
- Let João speak

2612
02:21:43,196 --> 02:21:46,114
- Speak João

2613
02:21:46,264 --> 02:21:49,297
Are there four
vacancies in purgatory?

2614
02:21:50,293 --> 02:21:53,192
- Yes.
- So put these four in there!

2615
02:21:54,176 --> 02:21:56,798
It's a great solution, my Son.

2616
02:21:56,970 --> 02:22:01,213
They can pay as much as
did and still secures their salvation.

2617
02:22:01,238 --> 02:22:03,417
And it has the advantage of
displease this fellow here...

2618
02:22:03,442 --> 02:22:05,147
which is worse than snake meat.

2619
02:22:05,172 --> 02:22:07,496
See him here from the back?

2620
02:22:07,521 --> 02:22:10,002
- I am!
-This is bad!

2621
02:22:12,489 --> 02:22:18,011
- My mother, what do you think?
- Oh, I would be very pleased.

2622
02:22:18,277 --> 02:22:19,740
So it's granted.

2623
02:22:21,563 --> 02:22:23,292
You four can go.

2624
02:22:24,932 --> 02:22:26,392
Oh, no way!

2625
02:22:26,435 --> 02:22:29,187
Man, that woman rules.

2626
02:22:29,212 --> 02:22:30,975
And now we, João Grilo.

2627
02:22:31,072 --> 02:22:33,971
At least this
I insist on taking it.

2628
02:22:34,116 --> 02:22:38,780
You who are so known, what is that
do you have to say in your defense?

2629
02:22:38,805 --> 02:22:41,001
- Nothing, sir!
- Nothing?

2630
02:22:41,181 --> 02:22:44,500
- The moment of truth has arrived!
- That's why I'm chipped.

2631
02:22:44,668 --> 02:22:48,107
- With me there were many lies.
- I'm glad you recognize it!

2632
02:22:51,244 --> 02:22:54,967
- You lied to survive, João!
- But I liked it too.

2633
02:22:54,992 --> 02:22:57,284
I ended up getting a taste
to deceive those people.

2634
02:22:57,309 --> 02:22:58,788
But because they exploited you!

2635
02:22:58,813 --> 02:23:01,098
Cleverness is the
poor man's courage!

2636
02:23:01,819 --> 02:23:05,320
Cleverness was the only weapon which
you had against the bad bosses!

2637
02:23:05,577 --> 02:23:09,718
Thank you for your intervention. But I must
recognize that I didn't live like a saint.

2638
02:23:09,824 --> 02:23:14,616
You are being humble
for her to take your pains.

2639
02:23:15,017 --> 02:23:17,396
The way I'm bad,
it might even be it.

2640
02:23:17,421 --> 02:23:18,729
No! Don't give in!

2641
02:23:18,887 --> 02:23:22,051
João, this is the father of lies!
He's trying to confuse you!

2642
02:23:22,234 --> 02:23:24,066
The truth is I don't
I was no saint...

2643
02:23:24,091 --> 02:23:27,176
and I didn't even die a glorious death,
like my companions.

2644
02:23:28,001 --> 02:23:30,520
João was a poor man like us, my Son.

2645
02:23:30,944 --> 02:23:35,713
And had to endure the greatest hardships
of a dry and poor land like ours.

2646
02:23:36,168 --> 02:23:38,394
Fought for his life since he was a kid.

2647
02:23:39,435 --> 02:23:41,188
Passed without feeling his childhood.

2648
02:23:42,282 --> 02:23:45,207
He got used for few bread and a lot of sweat.

2649
02:23:46,930 --> 02:23:51,593
In the drought, he ate macambira,
drinked the juice of xiquexique.

2650
02:23:53,741 --> 02:23:54,893
He felt hunger.

2651
02:23:57,069 --> 02:23:58,792
And when he couldn't anymore, prayed.

2652
02:24:00,814 --> 02:24:04,331
When the pray couldn't do anything, he joined a group of migrants...

2653
02:24:04,356 --> 02:24:06,269
who tried to survivie at the Coast.

2654
02:24:07,430 --> 02:24:08,430
Humiliated,

2655
02:24:10,326 --> 02:24:11,326
defeated,

2656
02:24:13,015 --> 02:24:14,300
missing a lot.

2657
02:24:16,360 --> 02:24:20,264
And when he got the news of rain, he took the way back.

2658
02:24:20,814 --> 02:24:21,814
Cheered himself again,

2659
02:24:22,772 --> 02:24:26,104
like the hope was a plant that grows with the rain.

2660
02:24:27,345 --> 02:24:30,312
And when looked again at his city, he thanked God...

2661
02:24:30,410 --> 02:24:32,536
for being a poor countryside,

2662
02:24:32,683 --> 02:24:34,985
but brave and with a lot of faith.

2663
02:24:37,666 --> 02:24:40,428
I ask you a lot for just not condemn him.

2664
02:24:41,908 --> 02:24:42,908
This case is hard.

2665
02:24:44,218 --> 02:24:48,290
I comprehend the situation that João lived, but this also has a limit.

2666
02:24:49,113 --> 02:24:50,795
I don't think that I can save him.

2667
02:24:52,842 --> 02:24:55,552
Give him, my Son, another opportunity.

2668
02:24:56,651 --> 02:24:59,006
- How?
- Let João go back.

2669
02:25:00,521 --> 02:25:03,402
- Are you satisfied?
- Oh, a lot!

2670
02:25:03,427 --> 02:25:06,566
For me it's even better, because from here to there
I'm careful when I die...

2671
02:25:06,591 --> 02:25:09,253
and I don't even go through purgatory,
that not to give taste to the demon.

2672
02:25:09,278 --> 02:25:12,517
- So, João. Are you satisfied?
- I am...

2673
02:25:12,542 --> 02:25:14,804
who must be damned
is the brooder's son!

2674
02:25:27,421 --> 02:25:29,228
What did he have, my God?

2675
02:25:29,253 --> 02:25:31,291
In anger, looked at you and saw me!

2676
02:25:34,423 --> 02:25:38,453
- You mean I can come back?
- Yes, João. Go with God!

2677
02:25:38,587 --> 02:25:41,692
With God and with the Wholy Mother,
which was who helped me.

2678
02:25:42,464 --> 02:25:43,464
See you later,

2679
02:25:45,012 --> 02:25:46,375
great Lawyer,

2680
02:25:46,720 --> 02:25:49,706
and don't let me down, no. I am
decided to take care...

2681
02:25:49,731 --> 02:25:53,218
but the Lady knows that the flesh is weak!
- Goodbye, João!

2682
02:25:55,219 --> 02:25:56,270
Thank you sir!

2683
02:25:58,397 --> 02:26:00,799
- See you later.
- See you later, João.

2684
02:26:01,118 --> 02:26:02,763
- João!
- Sir?

2685
02:26:03,092 --> 02:26:05,477
Whatch out you behavior!

2686
02:26:06,697 --> 02:26:07,697
Yes, sir.

2687
02:26:08,864 --> 02:26:13,170
Mom, if you continue to intrude like this for everyone,

2688
02:26:13,195 --> 02:26:15,936
hell will end being a public repartition.

2689
02:26:16,416 --> 02:26:17,416
Exist...

2690
02:26:17,812 --> 02:26:19,081
but doesn't work.

2691
02:26:34,054 --> 02:26:36,009
Look Chicó burying a dead body.

2692
02:26:37,648 --> 02:26:39,714
But what am I doing up here?

2693
02:26:40,534 --> 02:26:43,598
Eita! But what am I doing down there?

2694
02:26:51,438 --> 02:26:53,503
When I think that poor João didn't even had the right...

2695
02:26:53,527 --> 02:26:55,461
for a burial in the cemetery like the others.

2696
02:26:56,726 --> 02:26:59,699
Poor man, he is more abandoned than the Baker's dog.

2697
02:26:59,724 --> 02:27:04,661
An Our Father and a Hail Mary
for a soul that is sorry here.

2698
02:27:04,689 --> 02:27:06,369
Oh my God, it's João!

2699
02:27:07,886 --> 02:27:11,359
João! Tell me what do you want,

2700
02:27:11,568 --> 02:27:15,089
If you are in heaven, in hell or in the purgatory!

2701
02:27:15,390 --> 02:27:18,042
Look at this bullshit, this is soon a soul speech.

2702
02:27:18,547 --> 02:27:22,513
“João, tell me if you are, I-don't-know-what”.

2703
02:27:22,538 --> 02:27:24,977
Be ashamed Chicó!
I'm alive.

2704
02:27:25,774 --> 02:27:28,816
It's the bad souls, that says they are alive!

2705
02:27:28,841 --> 02:27:29,762
Oh my Holy Mary!

2706
02:27:29,787 --> 02:27:32,861
Get up Chicó! Can you see that is me? I'm alive dude!

2707
02:27:32,886 --> 02:27:35,399
- And is it possible?
- Well if it's possible that I'm right here.

2708
02:27:35,424 --> 02:27:37,656
- I just believe seeing it!
- Well just look.

2709
02:27:43,149 --> 02:27:45,679
What is it man, didn't you say that you just believe if you see it?

2710
02:27:45,704 --> 02:27:47,458
Yes, but you needn't show me.

2711
02:27:47,483 --> 02:27:49,221
And how this is going to be now, Chicó?

2712
02:27:49,246 --> 02:27:52,028
It's going to be this way. Me without believing it, and you without showing me!

2713
02:27:52,053 --> 02:27:54,657
And our society, our old friendship?

2714
02:27:54,958 --> 02:27:56,797
- Are they going to end?
- The had already ended!

2715
02:27:56,894 --> 02:27:59,877
It's against my principles make a society with soemeone dead!

2716
02:27:59,902 --> 02:28:01,915
But I'm alive, dude!

2717
02:28:02,329 --> 02:28:04,307
Look, take my arm.

2718
02:28:05,371 --> 02:28:07,453
Bravery man, take it!

2719
02:28:14,773 --> 02:28:15,916
You're right, João!

2720
02:28:19,016 --> 02:28:20,884
- How is that, João?
- I don't know.

2721
02:28:20,909 --> 02:28:22,359
I think the bullet grazed me.

2722
02:28:22,384 --> 02:28:25,892
My vision started to get blurry, when I woke up, I was here. Alive!

2723
02:28:25,992 --> 02:28:28,891
- Eita that's good news!
- I have a horrible one to give you.

2724
02:28:28,916 --> 02:28:31,379
- And what is it, man?
- I lost the money that was on my pocket.

2725
02:28:31,516 --> 02:28:32,777
Relax, João.

2726
02:28:33,178 --> 02:28:35,131
I took it out of your pocket before burying you.

2727
02:28:35,159 --> 02:28:38,057
Damn you rascal. With pitty of me, but didn't forget the money, did you?

2728
02:28:38,082 --> 02:28:41,003
Do you want to know something? Yes!
The money was there, you were dead.

2729
02:28:41,028 --> 02:28:43,155
It wasn't going to be useful for anything, so I thought it would be safer if it was with me.

2730
02:28:43,198 --> 02:28:44,924
You did good, I would have done the same.

2731
02:28:46,855 --> 02:28:50,164
- It means that we are rich!
- You mean millionaires!

2732
02:28:50,207 --> 02:28:53,378
Besides the bishop's and the priest's money, we have the money that Severino took from the bakery.

2733
02:28:53,620 --> 02:28:54,803
What do you think if we stayed with the bakery?

2734
02:28:54,871 --> 02:28:55,871
Great idea!

2735
02:28:55,938 --> 02:28:57,071
"Miramar Bakery:

2736
02:28:57,096 --> 02:28:59,493
João Grilo, Chicó e Cia”!

2737
02:28:59,518 --> 02:29:01,379
- What do you think?
- Beautiful...

2738
02:29:02,348 --> 02:29:06,101
Oh my God! My Our Lady! Stupid, stupid, stupid!

2739
02:29:06,126 --> 02:29:08,065
What's that?  What stupid? The stupid is you!

2740
02:29:08,090 --> 02:29:11,136
Yes, I am, João! I am the stupidest that ever existed in history!

2741
02:29:11,161 --> 02:29:14,491
- Oh my God my Whole Mary!
- What happend, dude?

2742
02:29:14,519 --> 02:29:18,407
Poor me, poor João Grilo! Were rich ate this moment, now are poor again!

2743
02:29:18,654 --> 02:29:22,504
- Don't tell me you lose the money!
- I lost anything João, it's here!

2744
02:29:23,245 --> 02:29:25,003
My God, my Whole Mary!

2745
02:29:25,028 --> 02:29:27,730
- And why are you shouting, man of God?

2746
02:29:27,755 --> 02:29:29,566
I thought you had died, João!

2747
02:29:29,677 --> 02:29:31,024
And what's up with that, man?

2748
02:29:31,107 --> 02:29:32,830
What is up is that me, thinking you were dead,

2749
02:29:32,855 --> 02:29:35,582
promised to give Whole Mary  all of the money if you escaped!

2750
02:29:35,633 --> 02:29:38,977
Oh my God! Oh my Whole Mary

2751
02:29:39,002 --> 02:29:40,741
Oh my God! Oh my Blessed Virgin!

2752
02:29:40,958 --> 02:29:44,085
But Chicó, how did you make a promise like this?

2753
02:29:44,110 --> 02:29:45,992
And would I know that you'd escape, disgrace?

2754
02:29:46,017 --> 02:29:48,197
Oh man hard to die, my God!

2755
02:29:48,222 --> 02:29:50,423
Oh, wretched promise!

2756
02:29:50,660 --> 02:29:54,296
- Oh, hopeless promise!
- Now is too late to say that!

2757
02:29:54,448 --> 02:29:57,702
- Wasn't it half that you promised?
- No João, it was all!

2758
02:29:57,963 --> 02:30:00,346
Oh, wretched promise!

2759
02:30:00,611 --> 02:30:02,726
Oh, hopeless promise!

2760
02:30:02,751 --> 02:30:05,532
Devil of a complaint on top
of people from minute to minute!

2761
02:30:05,557 --> 02:30:07,642
Lets stop talking and lets pay what we owe!

2762
02:30:07,667 --> 02:30:09,804
We're not!
You will go!

2763
02:30:09,829 --> 02:30:11,973
I didn't promised anything, and half of the money is mine!

2764
02:30:11,998 --> 02:30:14,999
Yes, but when I promised it was mine, because I considered myself your heir!

2765
02:30:15,030 --> 02:30:17,710
I have nothing to do with it!
I didn't promised anything!

2766
02:30:17,735 --> 02:30:20,269
So stay with your part and assume your responsabilities,

2767
02:30:20,549 --> 02:30:21,993
that I will settle mine!

2768
02:30:32,081 --> 02:30:33,081
- Chicó!

2769
02:30:34,494 --> 02:30:37,006
- What?
- Wait that I will go with you!

2770
02:30:37,141 --> 02:30:38,772
- Will you?
- I will.

2771
02:30:42,313 --> 02:30:44,486
I was convinced that you were right, João.

2772
02:30:44,511 --> 02:30:46,207
Yeah, but it missed who would convinced me.

2773
02:30:46,364 --> 02:30:48,562
If it was for another Saint, we still could see if we could change something.

2774
02:30:48,793 --> 02:30:51,270
But you promised to Whole Mary ...

2775
02:30:51,662 --> 02:30:53,398
Who knows I didn't escaped for this?

2776
02:30:53,545 --> 02:30:55,771
- So will you deliver?
- I will.

2777
02:30:56,130 --> 02:30:57,130
Personally.

2778
02:30:58,749 --> 02:31:00,665
Oh my God, oh my Whole Mary!

2779
02:31:00,690 --> 02:31:02,076
It looks like a scratched record!

2780
02:31:02,221 --> 02:31:05,542
With all this mess, I forgot the money I promised to the Major!

2781
02:31:05,567 --> 02:31:07,582
You promise money a lot, Chicó!

2782
02:31:07,598 --> 02:31:09,612
Did you forgot you were the one who made me promise this money?

2783
02:31:09,773 --> 02:31:11,753
And even gave the garantee of the Major's right to take off...

2784
02:31:11,753 --> 02:31:13,240
a strip of
skin off my back!

2785
02:31:13,281 --> 02:31:15,631
Oh my God, oh my Blessed Virgin!

2786
02:31:15,662 --> 02:31:17,954
And now all the money will go to the Saint!

2787
02:31:17,979 --> 02:31:21,590
- Is it not possible to be half?
- No sir, you said all of it.

2788
02:31:23,768 --> 02:31:27,243
Oh, wretched promise!
Oh, hopeless promise!

2789
02:31:28,112 --> 02:31:30,225
You're stalling more than a chick standing line.

2790
02:31:30,250 --> 02:31:31,580
Tell me already if you have the money!

2791
02:31:31,733 --> 02:31:32,733
I have!

2792
02:31:33,566 --> 02:31:34,566
I mean, I had!

2793
02:31:35,797 --> 02:31:38,676
Is that I promised all of it for Blessed Virgin if João escaped.

2794
02:31:38,701 --> 02:31:41,557
If I knew I would give you this loss, Major, I would have really died.

2795
02:31:41,582 --> 02:31:43,297
If you don't have the money, it is not a problem.

2796
02:31:44,852 --> 02:31:48,042
Fulfill the contract with me, or I'll rip your hide!

2797
02:31:48,050 --> 02:31:50,425
Will you do such a disgrace like
this with your own son-in-law?

2798
02:31:50,450 --> 02:31:54,186
What son-in-law... To marry my daughter, you need to be rich or brave!

2799
02:31:54,211 --> 02:31:57,831
So it is resolved, because Chicó is the bravest man of Taperoá!

2800
02:31:57,895 --> 02:32:00,564
This one I will keep to laugh later...

2801
02:32:00,589 --> 02:32:02,726
when I get angry!
- Because of me...

2802
02:32:02,727 --> 02:32:05,380
He made Vincentão
and Corporal 70 ran at once!

2803
02:32:06,168 --> 02:32:08,981
I will give you the chance to prove that your are a real man, who likes my daughter.

2804
02:32:09,006 --> 02:32:11,325
You marry her and fullfil your contract with me,

2805
02:32:11,433 --> 02:32:15,122
or give up on her and I will forgive your debt!

2806
02:32:15,147 --> 02:32:17,855
Oxe, he won't give up!
Chicó adores me!

2807
02:32:19,118 --> 02:32:22,738
- Choose, man...
- You can arrange the wedding, my father.

2808
02:32:22,890 --> 02:32:26,688
- I still didn't respond...
- You don't even need to, I trust you.

2809
02:32:26,988 --> 02:32:30,326
- We will marry tomorow.
- Tomorrow I'll rip your skin off!

2810
02:32:30,351 --> 02:32:33,336
Do you know what it is, Mrs. Rosinha, I would like a lot marrying you,

2811
02:32:33,361 --> 02:32:36,624
but the truth is that I am more
loose than store door pants.

2812
02:32:36,649 --> 02:32:39,410
- Oxe, and don't I know that?
- How?

2813
02:32:39,435 --> 02:32:41,242
It's been a while since I found out.

2814
02:32:41,492 --> 02:32:44,864
But it was too late and I was already crazy about marrying you.

2815
02:32:44,889 --> 02:32:47,626
- Who said I have courage?
- The pig!

2816
02:32:47,651 --> 02:32:49,889
- The pig?
- The pig!

2817
02:32:49,914 --> 02:32:50,781
- What pig?

2818
02:32:50,806 --> 02:32:54,644
The pig that Mrs. Rosinha will gain as marrige present!

2819
02:32:54,669 --> 02:32:56,296
And does this pig has to do with my skin?

2820
02:32:56,321 --> 02:33:00,400
We get marry, my dad gives you the pig, you pay your debt and gets your skin free!

2821
02:33:00,606 --> 02:33:02,706
Chicó, you found a partner in love

2822
02:33:02,706 --> 02:33:04,891
and I found a partner in intelligence!

2823
02:33:22,337 --> 02:33:25,194
If you want to give up, I will take the lady back home.

2824
02:33:25,219 --> 02:33:27,839
Not even if you skinned me out
my whole body, Major.

2825
02:33:28,244 --> 02:33:32,368
- Even just one strip.
- So I will make a belt with it.

2826
02:33:33,483 --> 02:33:35,875
You may not be brave, Chicó...

2827
02:33:36,000 --> 02:33:38,400
but are good at pretending of being one!

2828
02:33:38,711 --> 02:33:41,792
That saint pig gave me a lot of courage!

2829
02:33:44,570 --> 02:33:48,495
- Don't forget that half is mine!
- What money is this?

2830
02:33:48,520 --> 02:33:50,408
This coins are from the never time!

2831
02:33:50,433 --> 02:33:54,445
Help me Holy Christ! That money
was collected a long time ago!

2832
02:33:54,470 --> 02:33:56,024
I doesn't cost a single penny today!

2833
02:33:56,049 --> 02:33:58,459
But how I didn't think of this before?

2834
02:33:58,484 --> 02:34:02,278
Your great-grandmother deposited these coins on this pig over 50 years ago!

2835
02:34:02,303 --> 02:34:05,458
- How am I stupid!
- Imagine me!

2836
02:34:05,483 --> 02:34:09,457
I'm tired of this agony of becoming rich, becoming poor, becoming rich, becoming poor!

2837
02:34:09,482 --> 02:34:11,017
And I'm tired of this agony...

2838
02:34:11,017 --> 02:34:14,136
to be whole, to be without a strip,
to be whole, to be without a strip!

2839
02:34:14,967 --> 02:34:18,359
The party is really good, but it's time to fullfil the contract!

2840
02:34:18,384 --> 02:34:20,867
- It's soon...
- Don't worry...

2841
02:34:20,892 --> 02:34:24,029
That knife is sharp!

2842
02:34:24,131 --> 02:34:26,183
Wouldn't you have an anesthesia?

2843
02:34:26,305 --> 02:34:27,305
Wait, my father.

2844
02:34:28,639 --> 02:34:32,615
- What was on the contract?
- 10 contos de réis or a leather strap!

2845
02:34:33,247 --> 02:34:34,775
- 10 contos de réis...

2846
02:34:34,775 --> 02:34:37,233
... or a leather strap of him?
- Yes!

2847
02:34:37,915 --> 02:34:40,666
- Leather, leather?
- Leather, leather!

2848
02:34:40,989 --> 02:34:43,127
- Just leather?
- Do you think is little?

2849
02:34:43,191 --> 02:34:45,077
It's not little, but it isn't too much!

2850
02:34:45,102 --> 02:34:46,778
It's just a strap!

2851
02:34:49,220 --> 02:34:52,969
One strap, without a blood drop because blood wasn't on the contract!

2852
02:34:52,994 --> 02:34:54,169
What history is this?

2853
02:34:54,194 --> 02:34:56,959
The only word you'd pronounced on this contract was leather!

2854
02:34:56,984 --> 02:34:58,564
No one had talked about blood, hadn't it?

2855
02:34:58,589 --> 02:35:00,616
That's right, I didn't noticed this before.

2856
02:35:00,641 --> 02:35:02,579
Or you sir take a leather strap without taking the blood...

2857
02:35:02,604 --> 02:35:03,929
or you sir doesn't take anything off!

2858
02:35:03,954 --> 02:35:07,006
I should have bled you
by the neck, you bastard bitch!

2859
02:35:07,247 --> 02:35:10,494
I just don't do it, because the worst punishment
that I can give to my daughter...

2860
02:35:10,520 --> 02:35:13,958
is to let her marry
a disgrace like you!

2861
02:35:13,983 --> 02:35:15,518
Loose, poor...

2862
02:35:15,716 --> 02:35:17,770
- Clumsy!
- Kindness of yours!

2863
02:35:19,381 --> 02:35:22,536
Get out of here for the sixth generation!

2864
02:35:22,707 --> 02:35:26,082
I am able to
set fire to this house...

2865
02:35:26,107 --> 02:35:31,221
but I don't leave a penny for
lady, Mrs. Rosinha!

2866
02:35:31,930 --> 02:35:33,512
Everyone poor again!

2867
02:35:33,537 --> 02:35:36,002
Not again, my son.
This is my first time.

2868
02:35:36,027 --> 02:35:38,755
That's right my flower, you gave the
chest strike in reverse.

2869
02:35:38,780 --> 02:35:40,900
I was thinking if it wasn't better that way.

2870
02:35:41,307 --> 02:35:43,807
Who knows if I get rich I wouldn't end up like the baker?

2871
02:35:43,991 --> 02:35:46,108
And then with the misfortune, we get used to it!

2872
02:35:46,133 --> 02:35:47,816
Talking about it, I am getting hungry of the mullet.

2873
02:35:47,841 --> 02:35:49,765
Luckily,  I carried one
piece of the marrige cake.

2874
02:35:49,790 --> 02:35:52,526
Oh no, Miss Rosinha, you are already learning to be poor!

2875
02:35:53,527 --> 02:35:57,423
An alms for God's sake?
It's for me to take the belly out of misery.

2876
02:35:57,570 --> 02:36:00,407
Sir apologize us, but
belly in misery here there are already three.

2877
02:36:01,122 --> 02:36:02,122
Take it, sir!

2878
02:36:03,698 --> 02:36:06,401
- And go with God.
- And you with Him.

2879
02:36:06,673 --> 02:36:09,200
Oh no Miss Rosinha, it's gone
almost all the food!

2880
02:36:09,225 --> 02:36:10,819
Let it go, he is also a son of God.

2881
02:36:11,033 --> 02:36:13,498
Jesus sometimes disguises himself as a beggar...

2882
02:36:13,790 --> 02:36:15,417
to test the man's goodness.

2883
02:36:15,442 --> 02:36:17,858
It might even happen
but that one was not, no!

2884
02:36:17,883 --> 02:36:21,006
- Oxe, how do you know?
- Jesus? Black like that?

2885
02:36:22,033 --> 02:36:23,209
Why not?

2886
02:36:23,339 --> 02:36:26,099
I met someone in Cabaceiras that had met Jesus Christ.

2887
02:36:26,179 --> 02:36:28,286
- Where, Chicó?
- In Heaven...

2888
02:36:31,375 --> 02:36:33,680
Says that there the pilgrimage is a thousand times
greater than that of Juazeiro.

2889
02:36:33,989 --> 02:36:35,758
This dude told me he saw Jesus Christ.

2890
02:36:35,782 --> 02:36:37,924
sitting on the throne with a
bunch of little angels around,

2891
02:36:37,949 --> 02:36:38,949
just like in a painting.

2892
02:36:39,803 --> 02:36:41,484
He told me that
paradise is on the side

2893
02:36:41,508 --> 02:36:43,188
of Bahia, that's why Christ is black.

2894
02:36:43,372 --> 02:36:45,772
And how did he told you dude, if he was already dead?

2895
02:36:46,246 --> 02:36:47,246
I don't know...

2896
02:36:47,422 --> 02:36:48,422
I only know that so it was!

